INT. PARKED CAR, PARKING GARAGE LEVEL P3 - NIGHT

Concrete. Sodium light. A car idling, engine just above a whisper.

DETECTIVE CASSIUS ONWUDIWE-HARLOW (50s, stained trench, thermos in the cupholder) sits behind the wheel. Alone.

He watches an elevator door. It does not open.

He turns off the engine. Silence. A drip somewhere.

He picks up a cell phone. Dials. Puts it to his ear.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
Dispatch.

CASSIUS
Cassius Harlow. Badge two-one-four. I'm on P3 at the Meridian.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
Copy, Detective. Status?

CASSIUS
Stakeout. Nothing yet.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
Need backup?

CASSIUS
No.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
Detective, it's two a.m.

CASSIUS
I know what time it is.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
You've been there six hours.

CASSIUS
Seven.

He sets the phone on the dash. Opens the thermos. Pours coffee into the cap. Sips. Winces.

CASSIUS (CONT'D)
(to himself)
Cold.

He watches the elevator again. A light above the door blinks: 3. Then dims.

CASSIUS (CONT'D)
(whispering)
Come on. Come on, you son of a--

The elevator dings. The door slides open. Empty.

He sits very still. Then slowly lets out a breath. Closes his eyes.

CASSIUS (CONT'D)
(to himself)
Not tonight.

The phone buzzes on the dash. He picks it up.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
Detective, the subject has been detained at the airport. You're clear to stand down.

CASSIUS
Airport.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
He never came to the Meridian.

CASSIUS
Of course he didn't.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
Go home, Cassius.

CASSIUS
Copy.

He ends the call. Puts the thermos back in the cupholder. Starts the engine.

CASSIUS (CONT'D)
(to the rearview)
Seven hours.

He backs out slowly. The elevator door slides shut behind him on its own.
